From b09045ae5b4752c17c93a47a513bbaccf9701e2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: palazik <gochmyradov0@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:25:33 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 27/27] dodge: build Apple's open source HFS into the kernel

Port of dipa-studio/ios-sweet 0026 (credit: dipa-studio).

The iOS 16 root volume is HFS+ as far as this port is concerned, and on
Apple platforms HFS is a kext that IOKit matches on IOResources. dodge
loads no kexts, so link hfs-627.100.6 in instead and call
dodge_hfs_register() from bsd_init right after vfsinit(), before the root
is mounted; that function is the kext's start() sequence (converters,
vfs_fsadd, zones, sysctls, origin cache sizing).

The sources are fetched at an immutable commit by 0027-stage-hfs.sh and
never committed, like BearSSL and libpthread. They are compiled with the
kext's own view of the world (dodge_hfs_compat.h clears the kernel's
CONFIG_* options and lets HFS's kext-config.h decide), and the IOKit glue
is replaced: nothing is ejectable, no media carries an external journal,
no platform serial number, and no kext load tag to retain per mount.
Content protection stays off - dodge has no AppleKeyStore.

mockfs needed a guard to go with this. It serves a whole device as one
executable and would otherwise claim any device offered to mountroot,
including the HFS root; it now checks for a Mach-O header first and
leaves anything else to the next filesystem, which is also what upstream's
TODO there asked for.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
